BT 1 0 0 1 0 62 Tm .6739 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (To quickly get the status of your cloud\222s control plane nodes, check the running system services in Horizon. To do) Tj T* 0 Tw .7039 Tw (so, log in as an administrator to Horizon and navigate to ) Tj /F2 10 Tf (Admin -) Tj (> System -) Tj (> System Information) Tj /F1 10 Tf (. On this page) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.186273 Tw (are tabs separating all OpenStack services, including the APIs, Compute, Block Storage, and Network Agents. A) Tj T* 0 Tw .122787 Tw (service\222s state is indicated by the ) Tj /F2 10 Tf (State) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( column. If a service is up, the value is reflected as \223Up\224. If a service is down,) Tj T* 0 Tw .361705 Tw (the value is reported as \223Down\224. Click through each tab to see each service\222s status. A good indicator that a control) Tj T* 0 Tw (plane node is down is if you see \223Down\224 under the ) Tj /F2 10 Tf (State) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( column for all services of a particular node.) Tj T* ET
